    "created_at": "2019-06-05T05:46:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-05T05:46:42Z",
    "body": "@domenic :\r\n> This does mean we're closing the door on being able to deliver feature policy via in-document mechanisms like `<meta>`, since by that time it'll be too late (the agent will already be in its cluster).\r\n\r\nThere's language in the [companion PR](https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-feature-policy/pull/313), which I largely borrowed from [the CSP spec](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#meta-element), stating that “policies in `<meta>` elements are not applied to content which precedes them”.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest adding something like \"or to the document itself\" there, but your comment makes me think there are more fundamental issues afoot. Why can't `<meta>`-delivery support a subset of HTTP-delivery's policies, _ala_ CSP?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
